[01:00.76] Down by the sea
[01:03.75] I found your hidden treasure
[01:08.32] 
[01:12.65] Just you and me,
[01:20.20] We overdosed on pleasure
[01:25.48] 
[01:28.76] Yonnies in the wind,
[01:33.50] We're ruggin' up for winter
[01:38.71] 
[01:45.89] Putting out the bins
[01:50.36] In cold and windy weather
[01:55.40] 
[02:01.08] Down by the docks
[02:03.97] Live all the silent sea-ships
[02:08.87] 
[02:12.22] Crates are stored on blocks
[02:16.36] 
[02:20.32] Where now only the rats live
[02:24.65] 
[02:31.48] Sail me down the river
[02:33.46] Till we reach the shore
[02:39.24] Diving into the center
[02:40.96] Eating out the core
[02:44.22] 
[02:47.41] Down on the beach
[02:51.66] Saluting Captain Benbow
[02:55.88] 
[03:01.58] Always out of reach
[03:06.96] It's quiet when the tide's low
[03:11.86] 
[03:16.15] Climbing up the cliffs
[03:21.03] You can see for miles far
[03:26.08] 
[03:32.24] The boat that ran adrift
[03:35.30] Is sitting on the sandbar
[03:39.35] 
[03:47.28] Laughing at the waves
[03:50.24] That storm the river mouth
[03:53.49] The ice is on the move now
[03:57.53] Creeping north and south
[04:01.35] 
[05:04.28] Down by the sea
[05:07.96] 
[05:10.81] I found your hidden treasure
[05:15.76] Just you and me
[05:21.16] 
[05:23.35] We over-dosed on pleasure
[05:27.62] 
[05:33.96] Listen to your heart
[05:35.62] Screamin' at the sky
[05:39.75] Can't you feel it tremble?
[05:42.93] Don't you wonder why?
[05:45.13] 